    finding "AT1" state="open" size="frame-sized" \
        text="`states=` on an entity was declared and never read. `undeclared-state` works off the \
            `state` field's `one-of=` alone, so adding `withdrawn` to `states=` changed nothing — \
            the schema attribute was decorative for the whole life of the record" \
        note="fourth in one session, after `when-state` (AS2), `needed-by` on read models, and the \
            audit exclude list (AS9). The pattern is now the finding: this engine has no way to \
            report a DECLARATION nothing consults. `praxis prove` does exactly that for rules, and \
            the same question about fields, attributes and config keys is unanswerable"

    finding "AT2" state="open" size="observation" \
        text="a rule about the SCHEMA cannot be witnessed by a record, because the witness is a \
            document and the rule reads the composed schema. a-state-vocabulary-is-declared-once \
            reported UNWITNESSED until the checker was made to read schemas the documents declare" \
        note="the fix was right for its own reasons — a repository's extension block deserves the \
            same rule as the method's — but it was reached by needing a witness to fire. A rule \
            that cannot be witnessed is a rule whose subject the witness mechanism cannot express, \
            and that is worth knowing before the next one is declared"
